<ProgramPage
	slug="rmpg"
	eyebrow="RMPG"
	title="RMPG Ontario — up to $5,000 for retail technology"
	description="What the Retail Modernization Project Grant covers, who qualifies, and why taking it spends your DMAP eligibility."
	h1="RMPG — up to $5,000 for retail technology, with one important catch."
	verified="31 July 2026"
	sourceUrl="https://www.oc-innovation.ca/programs/digital-competence-centre/"
	sourceLabel="Source: Ontario Centre of Innovation"
	directAnswer="The Retail Modernization Project Grant is an Ontario program administered by the Ontario Centre of Innovation through the Digital Competence Centre. <strong>As of July 2026</strong> it provides a matched grant of up to <strong>$5,000</strong> to Ontario retailers with a physical location open to the public, for technology such as point-of-sale systems, online payments, inventory management, CRM, cybersecurity tools and AI tools. Eligibility requires <strong>1&ndash;50 full-time employees</strong>, incorporation and operation for <strong>at least one year</strong>, and <strong>at least $100,000</strong> in annual revenue before taxes. The catch: <strong>you can apply to RMPG or <a class='link' href='/funding/dmap'>DMAP</a> &mdash; not both.</strong> Approval and amounts are decided by OCI, not Vitops."
	facts={[
		["Amount", "Up to $5,000, matched"],
		[
			"Who",
			"Ontario retailer, open to the public, <strong>physical location</strong> (not home-based)",
		],
		["Size", "1–50 full-time employees"],
		["Trading history", "Incorporated and operating ≥ 1 year"],
		["Revenue", "≥ $100,000 before taxes"],
		["Funds", "POS, online payments, inventory, CRM, cybersecurity, AI tools"],
		[
			"Excludes",
			"<strong>You cannot also take <a class='link' href='/funding/dmap'>DMAP</a></strong> — and therefore not <a class='link' href='/funding/tdp'>TDP</a>",
		],
		["Decided by", "OCI"],
	]}
	sections={[
		{
			title: "The trade nobody explains.",
			body: [
				"This is the most consequential thing on the page, so it goes near the top rather than the bottom.",
				"RMPG and DMAP are mutually exclusive. Taking the $5,000 closes the door on the $15,000 planning grant — and, because <a class='link' href='/funding/tdp'>TDP</a> requires a completed DMAP, on the $50,000 implementation grant behind it as well.",
				"<strong>So the real comparison isn't $5,000 versus $15,000. It's $5,000 versus a path worth up to $65,000.</strong>",
				"That doesn't make RMPG the wrong choice. If what you need is a point-of-sale system and online payments, the money is straightforward, the scope is small, and the DMAP path would be overkill for the project. But if there's a larger modernisation ahead of you in the next couple of years, spending your eligibility on the small grant is a decision worth making deliberately rather than by accident.",
			],
		},
		{
			title: "Where this fits for us.",
